o Accounting Firm Trek Thu, Feb 4 from 8:30am - 3pm Thursday, February 4th from 8:30am - 3pm March Mar 17 Event: Advance Your Career: Job Fair, Professional Dress & Headshots Wed, Mar 17 from 12:30pm - 2pm Wednesday, March 17th from 12:30pm - 2pm See more events Career planning isn’t just about résumés and interviews; it’s about discovering who you are and what you are capable of.  We are here to help you bridge the gap between being a student and becoming a professional.  From your first internship to your first “real” job, we provide the tools and the cheering section you need to navigate every transition with confidence.  If you’re looking for a path that feels like you , you’re in the right place. Co-located with the Center for Career Development in the Johnson Student Union is the: Office of Health Professions who supports Gustavus students and alumni considering health professions careers with prerequisite course planning, gaining experience, and graduate application assistance Center for International and Cultural Education who supports international students and all students interested in studying away from campus. I Want To… Explore Career Ideas Stop googling “what should I do with my life” and start here. Discover how your interests, motivations, and strengths, match careers and majors Browse career ideas and peek behind the curtain Chat with a Peer Career Advisor or Career Specialist about your ideas Talk to people doing the jobs you are interested in Try a job for a day Get involved on campus Gain Experience Build your story, from class projects to student organizations. Get hands-on experience Find an Internship Signature Experience Work on the hill Make an impact Get a mentor Apply for funding for your career related experience Unlock your network Create a résumé Write a cover letter or thank you note and build your personal brand Transition Off the Hill From your last final to your first paycheck – we’re here to help. Ace the interview Manage your pro