      "description": "Employment Opportunities - Human Resources | Gustavus Adolphus College Skip to main content Admission & Aid Academics About Student Experience Menu Admission & Aid Apply Visit Financial Aid Connect Close Academics Academic Catalog Academic Departments Advising Day Explore Majors and Minors Signature Experience (SigX) Close About Administrative Offices Facilities Mission & History Nobel Conference Stories & Events Sustainability Visitors Close Student Experience Where You'll Live Athletics Performing & Visual Arts Get Involved Saint Peter Student Organizations Close Visit Cost Apply Info For Current Students Parents & Families Alumni & Friends Employees Visitors Navigation search\" Close What can we help you find? Search Admission & Aid Admission & Aid Overview Apply Visit Financial Aid Connect Academics Academics Overview Academic Catalog Academic Departments Advising Day Explore Majors and Minors Signature Experience (SigX) About About Overview Administrative Offices Academic Support Center Accessibility Advancement Arboretum Athletics Department Book Mark Campus Activities Office Campus Safety Center for Career Development Center for Inclusive Excellence Center for Innovative Entrepreneurial Leadership Center for International and Cultural Education Chaplains' Office Counseling Center Dean of Students Dining Service Event and Conference Services Facilities Office Fellowships Office Finance Office Gustavus Technology Services GustieWell Health Professions Health Service Housing and Residence Life Human Resources Institutional Research & Analytics Kendall Center for Engaged Learning Library and Archives Marketing and Communication Motor Pool Parents and Families President's Office Print and Mail Provost Office Registrar Research and Sponsored Programs Student Employment Summer Camps and Events Tennis and Life Camps Title IX Undergraduate Research Writing Center Facilities Mission & History Nobel Conference Stories & Events Sustainability Visitors Student Experience Student Experience Overview Where You'll Live Athletics Performing & Visual Arts Get Involved Saint Peter Student Organizations Visit Cost Apply Info For Current Students Parents & Families Alumni & Friends Employees Visitors Home About Administrative Offices Human Resources Employment Opportunities - Human Resources Human Resources Employment Opportunities In this Section / Human Resources Benefits Campus Perks Current Employees Employment Opportunities Join the Gustavus Community Gustavus Adolphus College is an undergraduate, residential, liberal arts college located in Saint Peter, Minnesota. Explore current job openings at Gustavus as HR guides candidates through the employment application process. Learn more about Gustavus Additional Perks Current Openings The City of Saint Peter Saint Peter is a city of approximately 12,300 residents. Nestled in the Minnesota River Valley , it offers many of the amenities and attractions of a larger city without the congestion of a more densely populated area. Housing is affordable and the city boasts arts venues, restaurants, shopping, and outdoor activities. Other major attractions, including the Mankato and Minneapolis-Saint Paul metropolitan areas, are within driving distance. College/city relations are strong. Gustavus faculty and staff appreciate the opportunity to be active, involved members of the Saint Peter community; they serve the city in government and advisory roles and play an active part in schools, community art and theatre projects, and other civic organizations. Students also constitute another significant link between town and college, through an extensive network of volunteer opportunities organized by the College’s Campus Activities Office. Volunteer programs include tutoring in the schools, adult literacy and citizenship classes, elder care, and “Big Partners.” An increasing number of courses also bring students into the community in service-learning projects that address identifiable community needs. For additional information about Saint Peter, visit the City of Saint Peter website. Employment Verification and Hiring Policies Employment Verifications: 507-933-7505 or 507-933-6310 Student Employment Office: 507-933-7501 Hiring Policies Gustavus Adolphus College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. To that end, the Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Committee was formed to encourage diversity, equity, and inclusion at every level of college life. Gustavus Adolphus College is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Employment decisions at Gustavus are based on merit, qualifications, and abilities. The College does not discriminate in employment opportunities or practices on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, status with regard to public assistance or other categories protected by law. All employees are responsible for supporting the concept of equal opportunity and affirmative action and assisting the College in meeting its objectives. Gustavus will make reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with known disabilities unless doing so would result in an undue hardship. This policy governs all aspects of employment, including selection, job assignment, compensation, discipline, termination, and access to benefits and training. Any employee with questions or concerns about any type of discrimination in the workplace is encouraged to bring these issues to the attention of their immediate supervisor or the Human Resources Department. Anyone found to be engaging in any type of unlawful discrimination will be subject to disciplinary action, up to and including termination of employment. Should you have any questions regarding equal employment opportunity or affirmative action issues, please contact the Office of Human Resources at humanresources [at] gustavus.edu (humanresources[at]gustavus[dot]edu) or 507-933-7304 to make arrangements with your local HR manager to review our EEO Policy and/or the AAP during regular work hours, Monday through Friday. Reach far. Dig deep. Go Beyond. Visit Cost Apply 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 Academics Admission About Experience Athletics Fine Arts Careers Request Event Give Instagram TikTok LinkedIn Youtube Facebook © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College. All Rights Reserved Annual Security and Safety Report Privacy Statement Title IX Website Feedback"
